{
  "category": "Antenna Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its whiskers serve as antennas. By sending and receiving electrical waves, it can communicate with others over vast distances.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its tail to absorb electricity from power plants or from outlets in houses, and then it fires the electricity from its whiskers.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sneaks into people’s homes and steals electricity from their outlets. When your electric bill seems off, it’s the handiwork of this rascal.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its upper whiskers are sensors that survey its surroundings. Its lower whiskers are organs that shoot electricity.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Dedenne’s whiskers pick up electrical waves other Dedenne send out. These Pokémon share locations of food or electricity with one another.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Since Dedenne can’t generate much electricity on its own, it steals electricity from outlets or other electric Pokémon.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
